# Build context is the application/ directory itself (see
# deployment/*.yaml: `build: ../application`). Keep dev junk out of the
# image — before this file the prod image carried ~47MB of dev uploads
# under inputs/ and dozens of __pycache__ dirs.
#
# NOTE: dockerignore patterns are anchored to the context root; `**/` is
# required to match nested directories (plain `__pycache__/` only
# matches a top-level one).
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
# inputs/ is a volume mountpoint at runtime (named `uploads` volume in
# the hub compose, bind mount in dev). The Dockerfile recreates
# inputs/local empty with appuser ownership.
inputs/
